I fixed #1139 and committed it as 56b81a10. When credits run out, the REPL hint now says Use a local model: /provider ollama instead of /model ollama/llama3. fmt, clippy (-D warnings) and the full cargo test all pass.

Why the old hint was wrong: in src/dispatch.rs, /model only replaces the model id (ctx.agent_config.model = new_model.to_string();) and leaves the provider alone. So the old advice sent the next call to the same out-of-credit provider, asking for a model that provider doesn't have.

Why `/provider ollama` works, checked in the code: the switch handler in src/commands.rs first checks that the provider is in the known list, which includes ollama. It then sets both the provider and the model (agent_config.model = default_model_for_provider(new_provider);). In src/providers.rs the ollama default is llama3.2, the same model the -p hint names. So one command is enough; no second /model step is needed.

Tests:
• The old test that pinned the wrong wording is renamed repl_billing_hint_names_a_command_that_switches_provider. It now checks the full new hint text exactly, and checks that the hint no longer contains ollama/llama3 or /model ollama.
• A new test, repl_local_option_resolves_to_the_single_shot_model, checks that ollama is a known provider and that its default model is the one the -p hint names. This keeps the REPL and -p hints pointing at the same model.
• The -p hint test is unchanged and passes.
• As a check that the tests can fail, I briefly put the old wording back: the renamed test failed, then I restored the fix in the same command.

Only src/prompt/network_error_summary.rs changed. Searching src, docs and README.md found no other /model ollama suggestions and no other references to #1139, so no docs needed updating.
